post_install() {
    cat << 'EOF'
================================================================================
MMU VPN Tray - Post-Installation Setup
================================================================================
1. VPN Configuration:
   The package installs a root-owned configuration at:
     /etc/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf

   The tray prefers this file so that passwordless sudo can safely pin
   openfortivpn to a config the invoking user cannot modify. Do not make it
   writable by your user account.

   For a per-user config (development/testing only), create:
     mkdir -p ~/.config/openfortivpn
     cp /usr/share/doc/mmu-vpn-tray/mmu-vpn.conf.example \
        ~/.config/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf
     chmod 600 ~/.config/openfortivpn/mmu-vpn.conf
   Then point the tray at it with MMU_VPN_CONFIG and adjust the sudoers rule
   below to that exact path. A user-writable config plus passwordless sudo is
   equivalent to giving that user root access.

2. Sudoers Permissions (required for openfortivpn, pkill & resolvectl):
   Copy or link the sudoers snippet to /etc/sudoers.d/:
     sudo install -Dm440 /usr/share/doc/mmu-vpn-tray/openfortivpn.sudoers.example \
       /etc/sudoers.d/openfortivpn
   Ensure your user is in the 'wheel' group or edit the rule for your username.
   The rule deliberately allows only the exact commands the tray runs.

3. Autostart in Hyprland (hyprlua):
   Add to your startup commands in ~/.config/hypr/hyprland.lua:
     hl.on("hyprland.start", function()
         hl.exec_cmd("mmu-vpn-tray")
     end)
================================================================================
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    post_install
}
